}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Complete formulas.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The texts of this notebook and the meanings of the registry (section I.8) \
contain complete formulas, written in TeX between dollar signs, for example \
",
 StyleBox["B^{\\rm out}_{\\rm LL}=\\big(1+\\tfrac14h^{\\rm IDA}_{\\rm \
LL}E^{\\rm max}_{\\rm LL}\\big)B^{\\rm err}_{\\rm LL}",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 ". A second reader, defined in the next cell, converts them into boxes. It \
is built like the reader of symbols (tokens, read from left to right), and it \
knows what a complete formula needs: fractions and roots, sums and integrals \
with their limits, accents, matrices, delimiters, the names of functions, and \
the spaces of TeX. Four properties matter for the correctness of what is \
shown."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"833e2454-bd2b-48b8-b3eb-9cf133d37350"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The arguments of a command.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " In TeX an argument that is not written in braces is the single token that \
follows the command: ",
 StyleBox["\\tfrac12\\ell^{\\rm x}_{\\rm LL}",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " is one half times ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[ScriptL]", 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["x",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f6b6343-dd91-423e-a2b2-fd0709d37a87"],
 ", and ",
 StyleBox["\\sqrt2\\,\\ell^{\\rm x}_{\\rm LL}",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " is the square root of 2, times ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[ScriptL]", 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["x",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "49831f13-7775-459a-a8b2-09e498a581e7"],
 ". The reader follows this rule. The TeX importer of the Wolfram Language \
(",
 StyleBox["ImportString",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " with the format \"TeX\") does not: it takes everything up to the end of \
the group as the denominator and everything before the fraction as part of \
the numerator, so that it shows ",
 StyleBox["\\tfrac12\\ell^{\\rm x}_{\\rm LL}",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " as the fraction with the numerator 1 and the denominator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"2", 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[ScriptL]", 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["x",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bcfc5b0e-7d1f-45b0-8727-501ca9bd87bb"],
 ", and ",
 StyleBox["Q_{\\rm LL}=-\\tfrac12",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " as the fraction with the numerator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Q", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e65b01e7-82de-4711-a973-35b4df43d1f5"],
 " and the denominator 2; it also shows ",
 StyleBox["\\hbar",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " as nothing. The importer is therefore not used anywhere in this notebook."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"c2e77d76-9e92-42de-99bb-4c95b0f908fb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The alphabets.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Every letter is given its alphabet by an explicit style: the letter of a \
variable is set in italics, text written with ",
 StyleBox["\\rm",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " upright, ",
 StyleBox["\\mathbf",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " bold and upright, ",
 StyleBox["\\mathsf",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " sans-serif (in the typeface Helvetica), and the double-struck, script and \
Gothic letters are the characters of the Wolfram Language for them. A formula \
is set in the typeface Times, so that an upright roman letter (the label K of \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[ScriptL]", 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["K",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1cca79e4-b56c-4b65-81b1-b3c07488a55b"],
 ") differs visibly from a sans-serif letter (the matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["K",
     FontFamily->"Helvetica",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "3"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "81af94f1-31f9-4dbf-bd03-87afe31db3b3"],
 ") and from an italic letter (the generator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["K", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bca0adc3-a26e-41d9-b0a0-dfef423bb366"],
 "); the text around a formula is set in the sans-serif typeface of the text \
cells."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"9d103094-8a70-42b6-a9cd-565c66ee6713"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Names are not products.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " TeX sets neighbouring letters and numbers without a space. The front end \
of the Wolfram Language puts the thin space of a product between two \
neighbouring items of a row of boxes, and this notebook keeps that space \
between the factors of a product, as the Wolfram Language itself shows a \
product. Inside a name there must be no such space. The reader therefore \
joins neighbouring letters of one alphabet into one string (the letters ",
 StyleBox["SL",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["SU",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " in the names of groups), and it puts the character ",
 StyleBox["\\[InvisibleSpace]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 ", which has no width, between a letter and a number that directly follows \
it: the coordinates ",
 StyleBox["x5",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["x6",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["x7",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " of the main project (they occur in the meaning of the number of space \
dimensions, section I.8) are names, not products of a letter and a number."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"0b157f4f-3ee8-4cac-9cd7-82724293efd0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Nothing is passed over in silence.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " A command that the reader does not know, a missing argument or an \
unmatched brace is recorded: ",
 StyleBox["SL31TeXFormulaProblems[tex]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " lists the problems of a formula, and the list must be empty. The program \
that builds this notebook stops with a warning for every problem in a text \
cell, and test S-15 (section I.7) checks every formula of the registry."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"df0c9d28-8bcb-4091-9d1f-07f2daa4a393"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The function ",
 StyleBox["SL31FormulaReading",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " writes the boxes of a formula on one line (a fraction as ",
 StyleBox["frac{a}{b}",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 ", a root as ",
 StyleBox["sqrt{a}",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 ", scripts as ",
 StyleBox["_{..}",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["^{..}",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 ", a bold or sans-serif letter as ",
 StyleBox["<bf:b>",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " or ",
 StyleBox["<sf:N>",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 "), without the spaces and without the italic and upright styles. Two \
conversions of a formula show the same formula exactly if their readings are \
equal; the tests use this."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6253e361-28b0-4e24-bd69-3389a2b90bc2"],

